<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.Africa money mkt shortage rises to 9.79 bln rand.</title>
<headline>S.Africa money mkt shortage rises to 9.79 bln rand.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Reserve Bank said the South African money market shortage rose to 9.788 billion rand on Thursday from 9.650 billion rand on Wednesday.</p>
<p>Three-month NCD rates rose further to be quoted higher at 17.40 percent offered from 17.20 and 17.35 percent, while the 90-day BA rate also moved higher to between 16.70 and 17.00 percent from 16.65 and 16.95 percent previously.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
